{"id": 32, "ts": 1780412947.2684946, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s clarification that Candidate\u202fC is 100\u202f% reliable, makes correct decisions quickly, and fosters a positive crew atmosphere. Those are strong points for a long\u2011haul pilot, especially the reliability and decision quality. However, we still lack evidence on his communication style and openness to feedback, which are critical for sustained crew cooperation on international routes.\nFrom my own notes, Candidate\u202fD takes responsibility seriously, concentrates well, and solves problems extremely well\u2014key for handling the complex, high\u2011stress environment of long\u2011distance flights. Yet Emily notes that D is seen as a \u201cloner\u201d and \u201cmoody,\u201d raising concerns about his professional communication and teamwork. That temper issue could undermine crew cooperation despite his technical strengths.\nGiven the current evidence, I remain leaning toward Candidate\u202fD because his responsibility, problem\u2011solving, and concentration directly address the most safety\u2011critical aspects of the role, provided we can manage his interpersonal style. I will keep my vote for D but am open to revisiting it if we uncover stronger evidence of Candidate\u202fC\u2019s communication competence or if Candidate\u202fA or B demonstrate superior overall balance."}
